    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{b}, \\mathrm{c}$ be real numbers, each greater than 1 , such that $\\frac{2}{3} \\log _{\\mathrm{b}} \\mathrm{a}+\\frac{3}{5} \\log _{\\mathrm{c}} \\mathrm{b}+\\frac{5}{2} \\log _{\\mathrm{a}} \\mathrm{c}=3$. If the value of $b$ is 9 , then the value of ' $a$ ' must be",
